{{Use mdy dates|date=April 2026}}
{{Use American English|date=April 2024}}
'''Group F of the 1994 FIFA World Cup''' was one of six groups of four teams competing at the [[1994 FIFA World Cup|1994 World Cup]] in the United States. The first match was played June 19, 1994, and the final games took place simultaneously on June 29, 1994.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.fifa.com/tournaments/archive/worldcup/usa1994/index.html|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20131220184449/http://www.fifa.com/tournaments/archive/worldcup/usa1994/index.html|url-status=dead|archive-date=December 20, 2013|title=1994 FIFA World Cup USA|publisher=fifa.com|accessdate=July 31, 2014}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.rsssf.org/tables/94full.html|title=World Cup 1994|website=[[RSSSF]]|accessdate=July 31, 2014}}</ref>

The group consisted of [[Belgium national football team|Belgium]], [[Morocco national football team|Morocco]], [[Netherlands national football team|Netherlands]], and [[Saudi Arabia national football team|Saudi Arabia]]. Netherlands won the group, Saudi Arabia finished second, and Belgium qualified as one of the best third-placed teams. Saudi Arabia became the first Asian team to beat a side from Africa in the competition's history.

